 of a version conflict, you'll need to evaluate which version of the peer"," "," When set to `true`, pnpm joins conflicting peer dependency ranges with `||` and installs the highest version that satisfies any of them. For example, if one dependency requires `react@^16.0.0` and another requires `react@^17.0.0`, pnpm installs the highest `react@17`."," ","+Only semver ranges can be joined. Conflicting paths, aliases, or tags leave the peer dependency missing. Identical non-semver specifiers are preserved.","+"," ### dedupePeerDependents"," "," * Default: **true**"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm11/docs/settings/peer-dependencies.md","lines":["@@ -31,6 +31,8 @@ If there are conflicting version requirements for a peer dependency from differe"," "," In case of a version conflict, you'll need to evaluate which version of the peer dependency to install yourself, or update the dependencies to align their peer dependency requirements."," ","+With `autoInstallPeersFromHighestMatch: true`, pnpm treats conflicting semver ranges as alternatives for automatic installation. Conflicting paths, aliases, or tags leave the peer dependency missing. Identical non-semver specifiers are preserved.","+"," ### dedupePeerDependents"," "," * Default: **true**"],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"pnpm11/installing/deps-installer/test/install/autoInstallPeers.ts","lines":["@@ -83,6 +83,74 @@ test('do not auto install when there is no common peer dependency range intersec","   ])"," })"," ","+test.each([false, true])('installs identical file peers without synthesizing a range (highest match: %s)', async (autoInstallPeersFromHighestMatch) => {","+  const project = prepareEmpty()","+  const range = `file:${path.resolve('provider')}`","+  for (const name of ['consumer-a', 'consumer-b', 'provider']) {","+    fs.mkdirSync(name)","+    fs.writeFileSync(`${name}/package.json`, JSON.stringify({","+      name: name === 'provider' ? 'peer' : name,","+    